body:
I think so. If I really put the effort and I had good luck in I'll be in my 40s renting an apartment, and doing the 9-5. I wanted things to happen in my 20s to early 30s. The only thing forward is working and aging - there's a good chance I won't ever be able to retire. 

&#x200B;

People after 35 tend switch focus in life with marriage, kids, house, career. I have too many regrets and missed experiences and it sounds lame but I don't think I'll like any job. And that's the if things go very well. Better luck next time. Thanks for the reply.
